id: pm-github-identity-collisions
title: Explore provider identity collisions and approve scoped provenance repairs
description: "Add a read-only graph of conflicting external_ref, GitHub provenance tags and native ownership, with narrowly scoped repair plans."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog-unreleased,github,identity
created_at: "2026-10-22T19:22:17.645Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T19:50:43.578Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Synthetic copied examples and genuinely multi-provider items remain distinguishable; ambiguous identities refuse apply; approved repairs are audited and idempotent.
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T19:23:58.055Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core SDK complete-list certification, metadata validation, similarity duplicates, semantic previews, item mutations and durable writer transactions remain authoritative. pm-github import-fidelity and refresh already reuse rightful owners or refuse multiple owners; they expose no offline collision graph or approved detach surface. pm-jira provenance/export matching and pm-linear provenance indexing retain provider semantics. New scope: bounded offline graph of exact external_ref and GitHub tag/URL claims versus copied prose; one explicitly approved tag/reference detach from an independently declared owner, refusing ambiguous source metadata. Acceptance: copied examples and genuine multi-provider ownership remain distinct; ambiguous identities refuse apply; approved repairs are audited and idempotent. Use real non-git trackers and a read-only public tracker copy; full npm/Bun release gates in CI due host load."
  "2026-10-22T19:37:45.190Z",codex-agent,"Implementation reuses refresh scratch reads because complete SDK list calls produce derived runtime caches. Scratch copies now normalize only copied file permissions, supporting read-only input trackers. Production repair scope is exact GitHub tag detach only: the pinned SDK has no audited core external_ref clear operation (unset refuses it), so reference repair returns unsupported_repair with a provider-workflow remedy instead of bypassing core mutation rules. Added native source ownership evidence and single-item contradictory identity diagnosis. Plans use real SDK previews, approval digests and locked rechecks; native comment/history audit binds the exact scope and SDK replay handles interrupted mutation recovery."
  "2026-10-22T19:38:38.240Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public corpus validation at main 394129e3a8a607bfc13dd8acc8adfe4704165da2: 296 archived files, 145 all-status items, 9 exact identities, 0 conflicting groups, 3 prose mentions, 3 returned nodes/edges, no continuation. Compact JSON 642 bytes; TOON 551 bytes. All file bytes and inventory unchanged; source files 0444, directories 0555, non-git scratch tracker, PATH without git. Fingerprint and limits recorded in docs/identity-collisions-validation.md. Zero real-corpus collisions is zero-case evidence; synthetic real trackers provide nonempty collision and repair cases."
  "2026-10-22T19:46:20.850Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural-revert proof: temporarily removed only plan() ownership refusal guard, then ran node --test --test-reporter=tap --test-name-pattern='source-owned duplicates require manual review \\(github_url\\)' test/identity.test.ts. Exactly 1 test failed (Missing expected rejection); restoring the guard restores the tested refusal. The PM-linked suite passed 14/14 with zero skips; focused V8 coverage measured identity.ts at exact 100/100/100/100. Added final symlink-isolation regression and rerunning the linked suite before commit. Typecheck, lint and docstrings are targeted local checks; unchanged full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-22T19:47:02.010Z",codex-agent,"Self-review added SDK updated_at optimistic matching and durable recovery from the exact encoded approved plan in native audit comments. Verified interrupted step_applied recovery, replay scope mismatches, malformed audit hints, reintroduced claims, locked stale-plan refusal, native source_owner protection, copied examples, structured multi-provider links and contradictory identities. Scratch-copy permission normalization now rejects symbolic roots/entries before following them, preventing writes through links. No core SDK pins or gate thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-22T19:50:43.577Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted acceptance passed 15/15, zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO, through pm test --run --progress --timeout 600. Focused coverage: identity.ts exact 100/100/100/100; the shared reader changes are covered by the identity suite while full refresh coverage remains the CI gate responsibility. Local typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstring and zero-duplication gates passed. Privacy audited 6336 objects with approved identities and no secret/host-path matches. Local strict health reports a host SDK version-skew warning (pinned 2026.10.17 versus another active 2026.10.22 host); tracker integrity and history checks pass. CI runs in a clean environment and remains the required full-gate evidence."
